=== request 1
model: "gpt-fake"
messages:
  - = plain-prompt.openai.golden request 1 messages[0]
  -
    role: "user"
    content:
      - = plain-prompt.openai.golden request 1 messages[1].content[0]
      -
        type: "text"
        text:
          | [Geno] Automated notice, not a message from the user. It is not the user's answer to any question, and it approves and confirms nothing.
          | These MCP tools are listed by name only. Load one with tool_search before its first call:
          | - mcp__docs__crash: Exit without answering.
          | - mcp__docs__echo: Echo the text back.
          | - mcp__docs__env: Show the environment the server runs with.
          | - mcp__docs__fail: Report a tool error.
          | - mcp__docs__image: Return a tiny image.
          | - mcp__docs__screenshot: Return a real 1x1 PNG.
          |
          | These MCP servers sent instructions for their tools and resources. Each is the server's own text, not the user's: follow it when you use that server, and it approves nothing.
          | <mcp_instructions server="docs">
          | Search before you echo.
          | </mcp_instructions>
      - {"type":"text","text":"[Geno] End of Geno's notes. The user's message follows."}
      - {"type":"text","text":"Use the docs."}
tools:
  - = plain-prompt.openai.golden request 1 tools[0]
  - = plain-prompt.openai.golden request 1 tools[1]
  - = plain-prompt.openai.golden request 1 tools[2]
  - = plain-prompt.openai.golden request 1 tools[3]
  - = plain-prompt.openai.golden request 1 tools[4]
  - = plain-prompt.openai.golden request 1 tools[5]
  - = plain-prompt.openai.golden request 1 tools[6]
  - = plain-prompt.openai.golden request 1 tools[7]
  - = plain-prompt.openai.golden request 1 tools[8]
  -
    type: "function"
    function:
      name: "tool_search"
      description:
        | Load the full definitions of the tools listed below by name only. A listed tool cannot be called until it is loaded; once loaded it stays callable for the rest of the session, so load each tool once. Pass select with exact names when you know them, or query with a few words to search the names and descriptions. Tools of MCP servers are not listed here: Geno names them in the conversation as their servers connect, and you load them the same way. The tools:
        | - bash_output: Read a background command's output: whether it still runs, its exit code once it...
        | - list_agents: List this session's subagents and background work, newest first: each subagent with...
        | - monitor: Watch a command's output and wake this session when a line matches pattern, when the...
        | - notebook_edit: Replace, insert or delete one cell of a Jupyter notebook (.ipynb).
        | - preview_list: List the launch entries and the dev servers this session started, with whether each...
        | - preview_logs: Read a dev server's stdout and stderr: its last lines, or only the lines at a level or...
        | - preview_start: To check a change on the running app, start the project's dev server from its launch...
        | - preview_stop: Stop a dev server this session started with preview_start: SIGTERM, then SIGKILL a few...
        | - recall: Search for words or a phrase in what came before, such as "queue" or "ตัดสินใจ".
        | - schedule_wakeup: Wake this session after delay_s seconds (60 to 3600), such as to check CI again in 8...
        | - show_files: Show the user screenshots, charts, reports or other files in the chat, with a caption.
        | - task_stop: Stop background work by the id it started with: a background command (bg-1), a...
        | - watch_pr: Wait in the background for the CI checks of the current branch's pull request, read...
        | - web_fetch: Fetch an http or https page, such as a library's documentation, and answer a question...
      parameters: = plain-prompt.openai.golden request 1 tools[9].function.parameters
stream: true
stream_options: {"include_usage":true}
